{"units":[
{"id":"tsdb/db_test.go:TestCompactSelectedSeries_UnsortedDuplicateRefs","bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","confidence":0.85,"risk_signals":[],"reason":"New test only; it adds coverage for unsorted, duplicate refs and cannot affect production behavior.","headline":"New test: CompactSelectedSeries handles unsorted and duplicate refs","summary":"Appends three series, calls CompactSelectedSeries with refs that are reversed and duplicated, and asserts the call succeeds, the head ends empty and only one block is written. It is test-only, and its claims hold: the input [s3,s1,s2,...] really is unsorted, and all samples fall inside one 1000ms chunk range.","focus":[],"issues":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/head.go:type SelectedSeriesHead","bucket":"human","change_kind":"rename","confidence":0.7,"risk_signals":["public API","exported type removed"],"reason":"Exported type StaleHead is renamed, which removes it from the public tsdb package API that downstream libraries import.","headline":"StaleHead renamed to SelectedSeriesHead with generic seriesRefs field","summary":"The exported compaction-only head view StaleHead becomes SelectedSeriesHead, and its field now uses the renamed seriesRefs type. The type is now shared by stale-series compaction and the new CompactSelectedSeries path. Its fields are unexported and not serialized, but the exported name StaleHead disappears.","focus":["Whether downstream consumers of the tsdb package (Mimir, Thanos) reference StaleHead or NewStaleHead and will break on upgrade"],"issues":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/head.go:NewSelectedSeriesHead","bucket":"human","change_kind":"rename","confidence":0.7,"risk_signals":["public API","exported function removed"],"reason":"Exported constructor NewStaleHead is removed and replaced, a public API change for library consumers.","headline":"NewStaleHead replaced by NewSelectedSeriesHead constructor","summary":"The constructor is renamed and takes the renamed seriesRefs type; its body is the same field assignment as before. In this PR both CompactStaleHead and CompactSelectedSeries call it through compactHeadViewLocked.","focus":["External callers of NewStaleHead, and the fact that its parameter type is unexported, so outside packages cannot build one anyway"],"issues":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/head.go:(*SelectedSeriesHead).Index","bucket":"skim","change_kind":"rename","confidence":0.65,"risk_signals":[],"reason":"Pure delegation, renamed to call the renamed selectedSeriesIndex helper with the same arguments.","headline":"Index now delegates to head.selectedSeriesIndex","summary":"The method now forwards mint, maxt and the selected refs to selectedSeriesIndex instead of staleIndex. Any behavior change lives in that helper, which is reviewed as its own unit.","focus":[],"issues":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/head.go:(*SelectedSeriesHead).NumSeries","bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","confidence":0.75,"risk_signals":["reported value changed"],"reason":"Return value changes from the head-wide stale count to the number of refs in the view, which feeds Meta().Stats.","headline":"NumSeries now counts selected refs instead of head stale count","summary":"It used to return head.NumStaleSeries(), a global counter. It now returns len(selectedSeriesRefs.sortedByRef), which is right for arbitrary selections and for stale selections that exclude series with out-of-order data. The value reaches BlockMeta.Stats.NumSeries through Meta().","focus":["Any consumer of the view's Meta().Stats.NumSeries during compaction (sizing, logging) that relied on the old global stale count"],"issues":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/head.go:var selectedSeriesHeadULID","bucket":"skim","change_kind":"rename","confidence":0.6,"risk_signals":[],"reason":"Placeholder ULID for an in-memory compaction view is renamed and given a new constant; the value is non-strict parsed like the old one.","headline":"Placeholder ULID renamed to selectedSeriesHeadULID with new value","summary":"The fake ULID that identifies the head view changes from STALEHEAD to SELECTEDSERIES text. The string is 26 characters and is parsed by non-strict MustParse, just as the old one was (which also held a non-Crockford L), so it does not panic. It is only used as the view's Meta ULID.","focus":[],"issues":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/head.go:(*SelectedSeriesHead).Meta","bucket":"skim","change_kind":"rename","confidence":0.7,"risk_signals":[],"reason":"Receiver renamed and placeholder ULID constant swapped; structure is otherwise unchanged.","headline":"Meta uses renamed receiver and selectedSeriesHeadULID","summary":"The method returns the same BlockMeta shape as before, with the new placeholder ULID. NumSeries now comes from the changed NumSeries method, which is reviewed separately.","focus":[],"issues":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/head.go:(*SelectedSeriesHead).String","bucket":"skim","change_kind":"rename","confidence":0.85,"risk_signals":[],"reason":"Only the receiver name and the human-readable string used in logs and errors change.","headline":"String output now reads 'selected-series head'","summary":"The receiver is renamed, the doc typo is fixed, and the text changes from 'stale head' to 'selected-series head'. The only effect is on log and error text.","focus":[],"issues":[]}
]}

{"units":[
{"id":"tsdb/compact_test.go:BenchmarkFilterSeriesAndSortPostings","bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","confidence":0.95,"risk_signals":[],"reason":"New benchmark in a test file; cannot affect production behavior.","headline":"New benchmark for filterSeriesAndSortPostings across input fractions","summary":"Adds a benchmark that measures filterSeriesAndSortPostings with the isSeriesWithoutOOO predicate over 100k head series at varying input fractions. Test-only code, so a line-by-line review can be skipped.","focus":[],"issues":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/db.go:var compactHeadViewBeforeEvictTestingCallback","bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","confidence":0.85,"risk_signals":["package-level mutable test hook in production code"],"reason":"Test hook that stays nil in production; it only runs when a test sets it.","headline":"Adds a testing hook that runs before head-view eviction","summary":"Adds a package-level func var that compactHeadViewLocked calls between writing blocks and evicting series. It is nil unless a test sets it, so production behavior does not change.","focus":[],"issues":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/db.go:(*DB).compactHeadViewLocked","bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","confidence":0.95,"risk_signals":["persistence","concurrency","data-loss risk on eviction","error handling"],"reason":"New shared compaction and eviction path that decides when head series are dropped; mistakes lose data.","headline":"Shared head-view compaction loop with an append-ID watermark for eviction","summary":"Pulls the per-chunk-range block write, reload and evict loop out of CompactStaleHead into a helper that CompactStaleHead and the new CompactSelectedSeries both use. It captures committedAppendID before writing so that series which got later commits are not evicted, skips reloads for empty views, and builds a fresh BlockMeta for each range.","focus":["committedAppendID returns a low watermark (all IDs at or below it committed) and returns 0 when isolation is disabled","maxt is read before the watermark is captured; check that gcSeries skips series whose samples are newer than maxt","if reloadBlocks fails on a later chunk range, blocks from earlier ranges stay loaded while their series remain in the head","the inclusive maxt in truncateSeries together with the inclusive loop bound"],"issues":[{"severity":"low","title":"Watermark comment overstates the block guarantee for samples newer than maxt","evidence":"mint, maxt := db.head.opts.ChunkRange*(db.head.MinTime()/db.head.opts.ChunkRange), db.head.MaxTime()\n...\nappendIDWatermark := db.head.iso.committedAppendID()\n// Samples with appendID <= watermark are guaranteed to be present in some\n// generated block.","failure_scenario":"An appender commits a sample at ts > maxt after maxt is read but before committedAppendID() runs. Its appendID is at or below the watermark, but the loop stops at maxt, so no block holds that sample. Eviction is safe only if gcSeries rejects series with samples newer than maxt.","introduced_by_pr":true,"depends_on_unseen_code":true,"line":1768,"detail":"The comment promises that every sample at or below the watermark is in a block. That does not hold for samples timestamped after the captured maxt. The safety then rests on the maxt check in gcSeries."},{"severity":"low","title":"Reload failure on a later range leaves earlier blocks overlapping the head","evidence":"if err := db.reloadBlocks(); err != nil {\n\t\t\terrs := []error{fmt.Errorf(\"reloadBlocks blocks: %w\", err)}\n\t\t\tfor _, uid := range uids {","failure_scenario":"Range 1 writes and reloads a block, then range 2's reloadBlocks fails. Only range 2's uids are removed and the function returns before evict. Range 1's block stays loaded while the same series and samples remain in the head, so the data is duplicated and overlapping.","introduced_by_pr":false,"depends_on_unseen_code":false,"line":1806,"detail":"The cleanup only deletes the current iteration's blocks. This logic was moved from CompactStaleHead."}]},
{"id":"tsdb/head_read.go:(*Head).selectedSeriesIndex","bucket":"none","change_kind":"rename","confidence":0.85,"risk_signals":[],"reason":"Pure rename of an unexported method, struct and field; the body is the same, and the package must compile with all uses updated.","headline":"Renames staleIndex to selectedSeriesIndex with renamed reader types","summary":"Renames the unexported method staleIndex and its return and field types to their selected-series names. The logic is identical, so behavior cannot change.","focus":[],"issues":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/head_read.go:type headSelectedSeriesIndexReader","bucket":"none","change_kind":"rename","confidence":0.85,"risk_signals":[],"reason":"Renames an unexported type and field and rewrites its doc comment; the struct layout is unchanged and it is not serialized.","headline":"Renames headStaleIndexReader to headSelectedSeriesIndexReader","summary":"Renames the unexported index reader type and its refs field, and updates the doc comment. The type is in-memory only and never serialized, so behavior cannot change.","focus":[],"issues":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/head_read.go:type seriesRefs","bucket":"none","change_kind":"rename","confidence":0.85,"risk_signals":[],"reason":"Renames an unexported type and keeps the same fields; it is in-memory only.","headline":"Renames staleSeriesRefs type to seriesRefs","summary":"Renames the unexported staleSeriesRefs struct to seriesRefs with no field changes. It is not serialized, so behavior cannot change.","focus":[],"issues":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/head_read.go:(*Head).filterSeriesAndSortPostings","bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","confidence":0.85,"risk_signals":["concurrency","new selection path for series eviction"],"reason":"Generalizes series selection with a caller predicate run under the series lock; it now drives which series the new public API evicts.","headline":"Generic ref filter with predicate replaces stale-only series selection","summary":"Replaces the stale-only selection loop with a generic filter that resolves postings to head series and applies an optional keep predicate under the series lock. It returns refs in input order and in label order. CompactStaleHead and CompactSelectedSeries both use it.","focus":["sortedByRef keeps the input order, so callers must pass sorted, duplicate-free postings (CompactSelectedSeries sorts and compacts)","with a nil keep, series are read without taking the lock"],"issues":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/head_read.go:(*Head).staleSeriesRefsNoOOOData","bucket":"skim","change_kind":"refactor","confidence":0.8,"risk_signals":[],"reason":"Clearly equivalent refactor: same AllPostings input and the same OOO-and-stale check under the series lock.","headline":"staleSeriesRefsNoOOOData now delegates to filterSeriesAndSortPostings","summary":"Re-implements the stale-series lookup as a call to filterSeriesAndSortPostings with an isSeriesWithoutOOO && isStaleSeries predicate. That matches the old inline checks run under the same lock, so the result is unchanged.","focus":[],"issues":[]}
]}

{"units":[
{"id":"tsdb/db_test.go:TestCompactSelectedSeries_LateAppendDuringCompactionSurvivesRestart","bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","confidence":0.7,"risk_signals":["test asserts sample loss as expected outcome when isolation is disabled"],"reason":"New test only; it cannot change production behavior, though it records known data loss when isolation is disabled.","headline":"Test: late append during selected-series compaction survives restart","summary":"Uses the before-evict hook to append a sample with t=400 after the block is written, then checks that the sample is still there before and after a WAL-replay restart. When isolation is disabled, the test expects the late sample to be lost permanently. Reviewers should know that this loss is accepted behavior; the test logic itself is simple.","focus":[],"issues":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/db_test.go:TestCompactSelectedSeries_OpenAppenderCommittingDuringCompaction","bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","confidence":0.8,"risk_signals":[],"reason":"New test only; it covers an appender opened before compaction that commits inside the eviction window.","headline":"Test: pre-opened appender committing mid-compaction keeps series in head","summary":"Opens an appender before CompactSelectedSeries and commits it from the before-evict hook. It then checks that the series is not evicted and that all three samples survive a restart. It skips when isolation is disabled. It adds coverage and changes no production code.","focus":[],"issues":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/head.go:isSeriesWithoutOOO","bucket":"skim","change_kind":"refactor","confidence":0.8,"risk_signals":[],"reason":"Small predicate (s.ooo == nil) pulled out as a helper and used by the stale and selected-series filters.","headline":"Add isSeriesWithoutOOO predicate helper","summary":"Adds a one-line helper that is true when a series has no out-of-order state. CompactSelectedSeries, staleSeriesRefsNoOOOData and both truncate paths use it. It is trivially equivalent to the inline nil check.","focus":[],"issues":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/head.go:isStaleSeries","bucket":"skim","change_kind":"refactor","confidence":0.8,"risk_signals":[],"reason":"Stale-NaN check moved out of gcStaleSeries into a helper with identical logic.","headline":"Extract stale-NaN last-value check into isStaleSeries","summary":"The float, histogram and float-histogram stale-NaN checks are the same as the removed inline code in gcStaleSeries. The helper is now used for filtering, eviction predicates and counting deleted stale series. Since the logic is unchanged, a line-by-line review is not needed.","focus":[],"issues":[]},
{"id":"tsdb/head.go:(*Head).truncateStaleSeries","bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","confidence":0.85,"risk_signals":["eviction predicate changed","concurrency with appenders","data loss risk"],"reason":"Changes which stale series are evicted and written as WAL tombstones; mistakes there lose data.","headline":"truncateStaleSeries skips series with appendIDs above watermark","summary":"Stale-series eviction now goes through the generic truncateSeries with a predicate: no OOO data, still stale, and no appendID above the watermark. The extra watermark guard keeps series that got samples after the block write began, so they are not tombstoned. Tests pass math.MaxUint64 to turn the guard off.","focus":["Which value compactHeadViewLocked passes as appendIDWatermark (lastAppendID vs committedAppendID), and that it is captured before the block write","The guard is a no-op when isolation is disabled, so concurrent writes to stale series can still be lost","truncateSeries now evicts when MinTime == maxt (it used to return early)"],"issues":[{"severity":"low","title":"Doc says watermark is lastAppendID; test says that would be wrong","evidence":"// appendIDWatermark is the lastAppendID captured before the upstream block write.","failure_scenario":"An appender opened before compaction holds an appendID <= lastAppendID and commits during the write window. If the watermark really were lastAppendID, hasAppendIDAbove would return false and the late sample would be evicted and tombstoned. TestCompactSelectedSeries_OpenAppenderCommittingDuringCompaction says lastAppendID would wrongly cover it, so either this doc is out of date or the caller is wrong.","detail":"The doc comment disagrees with the PR's own test about what the watermark is; the caller in compactHeadViewLocked is not shown.","introduced_by_pr":true,"depends_on_unseen_code":true,"line":1284}]},
{"id":"tsdb/head.go:(*Head).truncateSelectedSeries","bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","confidence":0.9,"risk_signals":["new eviction path for non-stale series","WAL tombstones","concurrency with appenders","public API consumer (Mimir)"],"reason":"New path that evicts and tombstones live non-stale series; a wrong predicate means permanent sample loss.","headline":"New truncateSelectedSeries evicts chosen series without OOO data","summary":"Evicts the given series when they have no OOO data and no appendID above the watermark, and writes WAL tombstones for them. Unlike the stale path, the series do not need to be stale, so with isolation disabled any concurrent append to a selected series is lost after eviction.","focus":["The watermark must cover only appends that were committed before the block write (see the open-appender test)","With isolation disabled there is no guard; check that callers such as Mimir really guarantee no writes to these series","Samples with timestamp > maxt are protected only by gcSeries' maxTime check"],"issues":[{"severity":"low","title":"Doc says watermark is lastAppendID, contradicting open-appender test","evidence":"// appendIDWatermark is the lastAppendID captured before the upstream block write.","failure_scenario":"An appender opened before CompactSelectedSeries commits in the before-evict window. With a lastAppendID watermark its ID is not above it, so the series would be evicted and the t=400 sample lost. The PR's test says lastAppendID would be incorrect, so the comment misdescribes the contract.","detail":"Either the comment is out of date (likely committedAppendID is used) or the caller uses the wrong watermark; the caller is not shown.","introduced_by_pr":true,"depends_on_unseen_code":true,"line":1297}]},
{"id":"tsdb/head.go:hasAppendIDAbove","bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","confidence":0.85,"risk_signals":["concurrency","isolation internals","data loss guard"],"reason":"Core guard that decides whether compaction may evict a series that has received concurrent writes.","headline":"Add hasAppendIDAbove to detect post-watermark appends via txRing","summary":"Walks the series' txRing of uncleaned append IDs and reports whether any is greater than the watermark; returns false when txs is nil (isolation disabled). The ring always keeps the newest append's ID, so a post-watermark append stays detectable. The claim about disabled isolation matches the code.","focus":["Callers must hold s.Lock as documented; check gcSeries' check closure calls shouldEvict under series.Lock","The disabled-isolation fallback means no protection; the doc says it relies on callers not writing concurrently"],"issues":[]}
]}
